// THE RULE IS THE TOWN'S, the same on every flat roof (each thing by the lot's own numbers). The small things are
// plain forms of few faces; on a lot under the far law (lv 2: buildHouses) the jars, baskets, pots and the ladder
// are left out (each under a quarter of a degree across from the nearest open place of the town): the mats and the
// bedding stay.
// P1: NEAR THE TOWN'S OPEN PLACES (lv 0) the roofs are the ones the visitor looks down on, and the town lives on them
// most where it is busiest: there nine roofs in ten have their drying mats, eight in ten their jars (up to three),
// six in ten their baskets and seven in ten their pots of herbs (elsewhere the shares are as they were). NOT ON A
